WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:05.280
Well hello there, SCP Fans! Let’s get&nbsp;
this out of the way first - You’ve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:08.520
seen the title and thumbnail, and&nbsp;
you’re probably wondering: Wait,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:14.820
is Siren Head an SCP? And the answer&nbsp;
is No. Siren Head is not an SCP,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:20.160
it’s a freaky internet monster created by&nbsp;
renowned Canadian Horror Artist Trevor Henderson.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:25.740
Your next question is probably: What’s with&nbsp;
this crazy-looking server bank behind me?

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:32.520
Allow me to introduce you to the Anom-O-Tron 6000,&nbsp;
the latest advancement of supercomputing owned and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:38.040
operated exclusively by the SCP Foundation.&nbsp;
It’s capable of a whole bunch of interesting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:43.320
features - calculating ideal containment methods,&nbsp;
running state of the art Foundation webcrawler&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:48.840
software, making and editing fun SCP YouTube&nbsp;
videos - but the most interesting feature that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:54.660
Anom-O-Tron has to offer is running hyper-advanced&nbsp;
simulations regarding all things anomalous,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.660 --> 00:01:00.000
with data fed into it by thousands of real-life&nbsp;
experiments conducted by the SCP Foundation.

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:04.500
It’s going to save countless dollars&nbsp;
and lives for Foundation researchers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:08.700
but way more importantly, it’s going&nbsp;
to let us explore all kinds of weird&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:14.880
and wacky What If scenarios that would never&nbsp;
happen organically. Could SCP-343 beat Goku,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:21.960
or Superman? Who’s a deadlier supernatural killer,&nbsp;
SCP-106 or Freddy Kreuger? Would the world simply&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:28.680
explode from adorableness if SCP-999 and Baby Yoda&nbsp;
ever crossed those multiversal barriers and met?

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:33.960
We can explore all of these questions -&nbsp;
Along with any others you may have down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:38.400
in the comments. Seriously, comment it.&nbsp;
We dare you! - but to get things started,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:42.660
we figured we’d make the Anom-O-Tron pit&nbsp;
the Foundation’s lankiest nightmare monster,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:48.300
SCP-096, against the internet’s&nbsp;
- Trevor Henderson’s Siren Head.

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:51.180
Sorry, Slender Man, you’re just not cool anymore.

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:55.560
So, without further adieu, let’s&nbsp;
kick the Anom-O-Tron into gear and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.560 --> 00:02:01.680
see how this wild battle plays out.&nbsp;
It’s time for SCP-096 Vs Siren Head!

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:05.340
Ricky and Eliot, a pair of aspiring&nbsp;
travel YouTubers from California,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:10.740
were taking a vacation to the Pacific Northwest&nbsp;
to spend some time in the area’s beautiful,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:15.420
lush forests. However, while the duo were&nbsp;
both big fans of travel for its own sake,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:20.700
they weren’t just here for the trees and fresh&nbsp;
air. You see, despite their jetsetting lifestyle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:26.040
Ricky and Eliot’s subscribers and views hadn’t&nbsp;
exactly been phenomenal lately. Turns out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:30.120
hiking vlogs and GoPro footage of the two&nbsp;
of them jumping into absurdly blue water in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:34.020
Bali weren’t exactly that interesting&nbsp;
to people who weren’t actually there.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:38.700
But Ricky had formulated an ingenious&nbsp;
plan to pull the two of them out of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:44.040
obscurity. They would hunt down and film&nbsp;
real footage of the legendary Siren Head,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:50.220
a supernatural monster said to haunt forests and&nbsp;
isolated graveyards. There were plenty of fakers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:54.900
out there on YouTube, but if the two of them&nbsp;
could get real footage of Siren Head - and also,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.900 --> 00:03:00.420
preferably, survive the experience - they’d be&nbsp;
framing their Golden Play Buttons in no time.

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:04.140
But they were already encountering&nbsp;
certain issues. For starters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:08.520
the two Californians had severely underestimated&nbsp;
just how cold it was in the Pacific Northwest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:14.520
and as such, were already shivering from&nbsp;
bone-deep cold. The second issue was food:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:18.960
While the two of them had thought ahead and&nbsp;
brought a selection of tasty protein bars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:23.520
they’d also gotten hungry during the early&nbsp;
hours of their walk, and eaten all of them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:27.600
leaving them feeling severely out of&nbsp;
luck by the time dinner rolled around.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:32.400
And the third and perhaps most problematic&nbsp;
issue of all was the fact that Ricky and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:37.380
Eliot didn’t exactly have a great sense of&nbsp;
direction. During all of their previous trips,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:41.100
they’d been on guided tours with&nbsp;
local experts. In this instance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:46.800
wanting to take all the Siren Head glory and clout&nbsp;
for themselves, they’d decided to come in alone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:51.300
with the incredibly janky Google&nbsp;
Maps app to guide them. As such,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:57.000
as the night was creeping in, the two aspiring&nbsp;
YouTube celebrities had no idea where they were.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:00.300
Needless to say, it wasn’t&nbsp;
exactly an ideal situation.

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:05.880
And to make matters worse, Ricky and Eliot&nbsp;
had been experiencing some strange feelings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:10.560
for the last couple of hours, when they’d&nbsp;
gotten particularly deep into the forest.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:16.620
That dread-inducing sensation of being watched&nbsp;
by something lurking just out of sight. A gaze&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:22.260
with some unknowable and darkly malicious&nbsp;
intent boiling behind it. These two poor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:26.760
saps had no idea what was in store for&nbsp;
them tonight, and wouldn’t you know it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:31.320
the one watching them right now wouldn’t&nbsp;
even be the only monster after them.

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:37.200
After an expectable amount of bumbling and&nbsp;
buffoonery, Ricky and Eliot managed to gather up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:43.320
enough tinder to make a semi-respectable campfire.&nbsp;
They could sleep out here tonight, then set off in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:49.620
search of Siren Head or civilization - whichever&nbsp;
came first - in the daylight the next day. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:55.020
duo did what they could to remain chipper, in&nbsp;
spite of the ominous circumstances. Sure, they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:59.400
were trapped in the depths of the woods, alone,&nbsp;
but think of the amazing vlog footage they’d get!

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:03.660
They’d be like the next Blair Witch&nbsp;
crew, except they’d live, hopefully!

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:09.840
But as the duo sat next to their campfire, they&nbsp;
felt that ominous sensation again. The hairs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:14.160
on the back of their necks started standing&nbsp;
up. They felt shivers that didn’t just come&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:19.080
from the cold. More and more, they started to&nbsp;
feel certain that something in this forest was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:25.260
watching them. Something ancient and powerful&nbsp;
and evil. That’s when one of them heard the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:30.060
telltale crackle of radio static, and their&nbsp;
skeletons almost jumped out of their skin.

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:34.140
Could it be him? The Patron Saint&nbsp;
of Going Missing Without a Trace,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:39.480
of Creeping Dread, of Bad Things&nbsp;
Coming? Siren Head himself?

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:45.480
Both men fell silent. All they could hear was&nbsp;
the crackling of their own fire. Had the sound&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:50.940
before just been an illusion? A product of&nbsp;
a pair of paranoid minds also predisposed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.940 --> 00:05:55.800
to sense Siren-Headed monsters lurking amongst&nbsp;
the trees? They’d been reading about a higher&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.800 --> 00:06:01.020
rate of disappearances in this area, along with&nbsp;
a number of frightening sightings of tall, thin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:06.360
beings and radio static that seemed perfectly&nbsp;
consistent with Siren Head activity. That’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:10.920
why they’d come here in the first place.&nbsp;
But had they come here to their deaths?

00:06:10.920 --> 00:06:16.380
The two needed to distract themselves or they’d&nbsp;
go mad from the paranoia. They decided to share&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:21.000
a few fun little anecdotes of the travels&nbsp;
they’d had before meeting one another, showing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:26.820
the photos they’d saved on their smartphones.&nbsp;
Ricky had been to Hawaii, Tahiti, Bora Bora,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:33.300
Fiji, St. Lucia, and the Maldives. Clearly,&nbsp;
he liked his vacations warm and sandy. Eliot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:38.640
on the other hand, tended to like his trips to be&nbsp;
a little more adventurous. He’d seen volcanoes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:44.640
waterfalls, deep and treacherous cave systems,&nbsp;
and of course, a little guided mountaineering.

00:06:44.640 --> 00:06:48.300
One photo that Eliot showed Ricky&nbsp;
was particularly breathtaking:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:53.640
He was standing in the foreground of a snowy&nbsp;
landscape, with an incredible mountain range&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:58.920
behind him. When Ricky asked Eliot where exactly&nbsp;
he’d taken this picture, strangely enough,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:04.320
he drew a complete blank. Maybe somewhere&nbsp;
in Canada, or Siberia, or something like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:09.240
that… But it was a hell of a trip, whatever&nbsp;
the case, he remembered having a great time.

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:15.240
It was such a tiny detail, but when looking at the&nbsp;
photo, Ricky couldn’t help but notice something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:20.700
in the background. A speck of white. Sure, not&nbsp;
exactly newsworthy in a snowy mountain range,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:25.200
but this wasn’t snow. It was a&nbsp;
speck of white that seemed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:29.640
be a slightly different shade than the&nbsp;
rest of the mountain. Strange. Perhaps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.640 --> 00:07:33.240
it was just some tiny particle stuck on&nbsp;
the lens whenever the photo was taken.

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:36.300
The two continued to chat and&nbsp;
warm their hands against the fire,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:40.080
having no idea of the horror&nbsp;
they’d just awoken in doing so.

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:44.460
Over a hundred miles away, at an&nbsp;
SCP Foundation containment site,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.460 --> 00:07:48.840
researchers and guards walked around the&nbsp;
perimeter of a huge, airtight metal cube,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.840 --> 00:07:53.880
reading off diagnostics and audio recordings.&nbsp;
For reasons that should be obvious to everyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.880 --> 00:07:57.240
who’s a fan of this channel, there&nbsp;
were no camera feeds coming from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.240 --> 00:08:03.300
inside of the great metal cube. Only a faint&nbsp;
whimpering sound, like a sad, wounded animal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:09.240
and the clanking of pacing feet moving back and&nbsp;
forth over the metal, dragging forlorn knuckles.

00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:13.680
It turned every head in the room when&nbsp;
the crying started to get louder. Soon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:18.780
it wasn’t just quiet weeping, it was a&nbsp;
series of horrendous, slobbering sobs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.780 --> 00:08:23.700
wails of pure pain and despair. Someone in&nbsp;
the room screamed “Close your eyes and hit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.700 --> 00:08:28.140
the deck!”, knowing exactly what had happened.&nbsp;
They’d learned well enough from the infamous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:33.960
Incident 096-1-A Containment Breach that there&nbsp;
was no way of stopping this thing until it’d&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:39.060
run its course. The best they could do was&nbsp;
minimize their own fatalities in the process.

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:43.920
Everyone in the room did as they were told,&nbsp;
hitting the ground, closing their eyes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:48.900
and covering them with their hands, just&nbsp;
to be safe. That’s when the solid steel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.900 --> 00:08:54.840
of the cube was torn open like crepe paper,&nbsp;
and the howling, raging SCP-096 broke free,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.840 --> 00:09:00.480
galloping on all fours through the nearest wall,&nbsp;
shattering it and spraying debris everywhere.

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:05.820
As Mobile Task Forces were dispatched to track&nbsp;
the rampaging abomination and try their best to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.820 --> 00:09:09.600
clear the path ahead as it sought out its&nbsp;
target, one thought was going through the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:15.420
minds of everyone in the room: “Woe betide&nbsp;
the poor fools who saw that monster’s face…”

00:09:15.420 --> 00:09:21.000
Back in the deep, dark forests of the Pacific&nbsp;
Northwest, the presence of some unnerving force&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:25.980
was becoming far harder to deny for Ricky and&nbsp;
Eliot. They heard the sounds of garbled voices out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.980 --> 00:09:32.040
in the woods. The squeals and crackles of radio&nbsp;
static. They saw shapes moving amongst the trees,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:37.980
tall and thin, like long, spindly limbs.&nbsp;
While neither wanted to voice their fear,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.980 --> 00:09:42.600
they were both thinking similar things:&nbsp;
If there really was a monster out here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:46.980
why hadn’t it killed them? It had&nbsp;
all the time in the world to do it.

00:09:46.980 --> 00:09:53.220
But that was just it, wasn’t it? It had all&nbsp;
the time in the world, so why rush? It had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.220 --> 00:09:59.760
every advantage. It could take its time, and do&nbsp;
this exactly how it wanted to. Ricky and Eliot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:04.500
had made themselves the perfect prey. And&nbsp;
as they saw a huge, lithe figure suddenly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:08.880
separate itself from the trees, they began&nbsp;
to wonder if it was really worth it to risk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.880 --> 00:10:15.060
both of their lives for YouTube clout. Either&nbsp;
way, it was now probably too late for regrets.

00:10:15.060 --> 00:10:20.040
Ricky and Eliot’s jaws fell in horror as the&nbsp;
monster emerged from the darkness before them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:24.720
They recognized the awful, mottled skin&nbsp;
stretched over the monster’s forty-foot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:29.700
frame. They saw the grasping hands, and&nbsp;
up above, the nightmarish, faceless head,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.700 --> 00:10:35.640
split into a pair of sirens pointing in different&nbsp;
directions, each one filled with gnashing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.640 --> 00:10:41.100
teeth and slithering tongues. It was even more&nbsp;
terrifying than they possibly could have imagined.

00:10:41.100 --> 00:10:43.320
Siren Head’s speakers crackled into life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.320 --> 00:10:52.980
and hissed out, “NINE. EIGHTEEN.&nbsp;
ONE. CHILD. SEVENTEEN. REMOVE. VILE.”

00:10:52.980 --> 00:10:56.280
Ricky and Eliot stumbled&nbsp;
backwards as Siren Head advanced,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.280 --> 00:11:01.080
its speakers still bleeding hateful&nbsp;
static. Neither could move or speak,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.080 --> 00:11:05.520
only watch as its long, gnarled fingers&nbsp;
reached from the dark to grasp them.

00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:10.740
There was a terrible pained wail in the woods&nbsp;
after that. But it wasn’t coming from Ricky,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.740 --> 00:11:13.980
Eliot, or Siren Head. It was distant at first,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:19.680
but soon became louder and louder as the force’s&nbsp;
point of origin came barreling towards them.

00:11:19.680 --> 00:11:26.400
Even Siren Head couldn’t help but turn to&nbsp;
see SCP-096, a flash of terrible white fury,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:31.080
come charging towards them in the dark,&nbsp;
knowing down all the trees in its path.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:36.720
Leaves and pine needles scattered. Trunks&nbsp;
exploded into splinters. Nothing would stop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.720 --> 00:11:42.540
the Shy Guy from claiming its prey. Nothing&nbsp;
would stop it from destroying Ricky, and now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.540 --> 00:11:47.280
as it approached, Eliot made the fatal&nbsp;
mistake of looking at its face, too.

00:11:47.280 --> 00:11:51.960
096 lunged, ready to go in for the kill,&nbsp;
when Siren Head’s hands closed around the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:51.960 --> 00:11:56.940
Shy Guy’s slender torso. In one fluid motion,&nbsp;
with surprising strength for its scrawny build,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.940 --> 00:12:02.040
it hurled the Shy Guy into the distance,&nbsp;
smashing another several trees in its path.

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:08.700
The words, “MY PREY. MY PREY. MINE. MINE. MINE,”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.700 --> 00:12:10.320
hissed out of its speakers.

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:17.040
But 096 was only down for mere moments. It&nbsp;
sprung back up on its hind and forelegs and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:22.140
started galloping towards Ricky and Eliot again,&nbsp;
who were still frozen in place. This time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.140 --> 00:12:26.580
just before the Shy Guy’s terrible claws could&nbsp;
close around the two hapless wannabe YouTubers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:26.580 --> 00:12:31.860
down came Siren Head’s clenched fist,&nbsp;
pounding 096’s head into the dirt.

00:12:31.860 --> 00:12:36.000
Overhead, Mobile Task Force helicopters&nbsp;
circled, wearing their SCRAMBLE goggles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:40.620
and trying to get a visual on the situation&nbsp;
unfolding below. They could hardly believe what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.620 --> 00:12:45.300
they were seeing down there. Was some other&nbsp;
unclassified anomaly managing to intercept&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:45.300 --> 00:12:50.700
SCP-096 in its rage state? Only a handful of&nbsp;
anomalies on record had ever been shown as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:55.680
being capable of such a feat. It seemed they&nbsp;
were dealing with something serious here.

00:12:55.680 --> 00:13:00.540
Down below, the battle continued. Siren&nbsp;
Head had a unique advantage over most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:00.540 --> 00:13:06.720
other combatants facing SCP-096: It was&nbsp;
an extradimensional being with no eyes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:06.720 --> 00:13:13.020
merely an innate psychic awareness of its&nbsp;
victims around it - not unlike how SCP-096&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:18.240
detects people seeing its face in photographs&nbsp;
or videos without need for any kind of direct&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:18.240 --> 00:13:22.740
contact. As such, it was impossible for&nbsp;
Siren Head to see the Shy Guy’s face,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:27.660
and thus, impossible for the Shy Guy to ever&nbsp;
actually direct its aggression against it.

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:33.900
Whether or not 096 would kill-steal Siren Head’s&nbsp;
intended prey was another matter entirely.

00:13:33.900 --> 00:13:38.160
In the night’s first minor miracle, Ricky&nbsp;
and Eliot remembered that they’d been born&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:38.160 --> 00:13:43.080
with working legs, and decided that right now&nbsp;
would be an excellent time to use them. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:43.080 --> 00:13:48.660
turned and began to run while Siren Head continued&nbsp;
beating the Shy Guy into the dirt, sprinting with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:53.160
all their might. However, the growing distance&nbsp;
between them only aggravated the Shy Guy further.

00:13:53.160 --> 00:13:58.500
It sprang out from the dirt with unstoppable&nbsp;
force and broke away from Siren Head’s grip.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:58.500 --> 00:14:03.960
The Shy Guy never wasted time, ever, it always&nbsp;
made a beeline for its intended victim with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:03.960 --> 00:14:10.380
one directive in mind: Total annihilation.&nbsp;
Tonight is no different. Ricky and Eliot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:10.380 --> 00:14:13.200
screamed as they heard its pounding&nbsp;
gallop on the ground behind them.

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:16.260
Closer, closer, closer…

00:14:16.260 --> 00:14:18.960
Then suddenly, defying all spatial reasoning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:24.420
Siren Head emerged out of the darkness between&nbsp;
Ricky, Eliot, and 096. Being forty feet tall,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:29.280
Siren Head dwarfed even the Shy Guy. It lunged&nbsp;
and grabbed the wailing white monstrosity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:29.280 --> 00:14:34.800
holding it as one would a particulary vicious&nbsp;
cat and trying to keep it in place. Siren&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:34.800 --> 00:14:39.720
Head wanted to crush this monster’s bones and&nbsp;
carry on stalking its feeble human prey - who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:39.720 --> 00:14:44.340
were currently in the process of getting&nbsp;
away - but somehow, that was impossible.

00:14:44.340 --> 00:14:48.300
It was almost like the monster&nbsp;
had an indestructible skeleton…

00:14:48.300 --> 00:14:52.980
Up above, the Mobile Task Forces continued&nbsp;
observing this clash of the titans from their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:52.980 --> 00:14:58.680
two helicopters. Seeing how Siren Head was somehow&nbsp;
doing a serviceable job of subduing the Shy Guy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:58.680 --> 00:15:02.400
one of the task force members joked,&nbsp;
“Maybe we should hire this guy.”

00:15:02.400 --> 00:15:06.600
Another chimed in, “I don’t think we&nbsp;
have any ballistic vests in his size.”

00:15:06.600 --> 00:15:11.820
The laughter soon turned to screams when Siren&nbsp;
Head hurled SCP-096’s flailing body up at one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:11.820 --> 00:15:17.100
of the helicopters with incredible force, knocking&nbsp;
it out of the sky. It careened down to the ground,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:17.100 --> 00:15:21.600
a ball of fear and violence, before&nbsp;
exploding. Anyone who survived the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:26.220
initial blast was unlucky enough to have seen&nbsp;
the Shy Guy’s face. Their screams rang out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:26.220 --> 00:15:31.740
briefly, before being abruptly silenced by the&nbsp;
monster. Helicopter Alpha had no survivors.

00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:36.060
Meanwhile, Ricky and Eliot had kept running&nbsp;
until their lungs burned and their muscles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:36.060 --> 00:15:41.460
pumped thumbtacks. Seeing that the chaos was so&nbsp;
far behind them now, they took a moment to stop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:41.460 --> 00:15:46.980
and breathe, recomposing themselves. In the second&nbsp;
minor miracle of the night, it looked like the two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:46.980 --> 00:15:52.380
of them had actually survived this ordeal. Those&nbsp;
two horrific monsters had canceled each other out.

00:15:52.380 --> 00:15:57.120
But Ricky and Eliot were about to learn a&nbsp;
harsh lesson: They really weren’t that lucky.

00:15:57.120 --> 00:16:00.600
The last thing the two ever saw&nbsp;
was Siren Head emerging from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:04.260
darkness once more. The last thing they&nbsp;
ever felt was the monster’s terrible,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:04.260 --> 00:16:09.180
gnarled fingers curling around their bodies,&nbsp;
too fast for them to escape. And the last thing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:09.180 --> 00:16:14.700
they ever heard was each other’s screams,&nbsp;
followed by a sickeningly meaty crunch.

00:16:14.700 --> 00:16:19.920
Elsewhere in the forest, SCP-096’s&nbsp;
wails died down to its usual maudlin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:19.920 --> 00:16:24.060
sob. The rage state had ended; all&nbsp;
of its targets had been destroyed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:24.060 --> 00:16:27.540
It just hadn’t been the one to&nbsp;
do all of the destroying, per se.

00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:33.000
Not long after that, Helicopter Bravo descended&nbsp;
safely and the remaining MTF members closed around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:37.080
the blubbering beast. Someone black bagged&nbsp;
it and everyone breathed a sigh of relief,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:37.080 --> 00:16:40.380
knowing that was at least one&nbsp;
monster taken care of tonight.

00:16:40.380 --> 00:16:43.320
“What about the other one?”&nbsp;
the MTF Lieutenant asked.

00:16:43.320 --> 00:16:47.400
The team’s commander shook his head and&nbsp;
said, “Let’s worry about that freak later&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:51.480
and get 096 back to containment.&nbsp;
This place gives me the creeps…”

00:16:51.480 --> 00:16:55.920
Now go check out “SCP-096 - Look at&nbsp;
a Picture of Shy Guy in Space? The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:55.920 --> 00:17:00.840
Shy Guy Questions and Theories” and&nbsp;
“SCP-096 Shy Guy ESCAPE - Incident&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:00.840 --> 00:17:06.720
096-1-A Containment Breach” for more wild&nbsp;
tales of the world’s scariest introvert!

